ACADEMY:alternatemouseinterface
"If you don't want to be bad at this game, try to be better."
END

ACADEMY:buildahero
"Jarmen Kell, Colonel Burton and Black Lotus can be priceless for your strategy. These heroes can turn the tide of battle alone. You can build only one hero, but do not underestimate his capabilities."
END

ACADEMY:buildallstructures
"If you think that your ally is the reason you lost the team game, then most likely the reason is YOU."
END

ACADEMY:buildbarrackssooner
"Purchase general's powers and research upgrades to increase your income. USA has Supply Lines upgrade. China has Hacker Training general's power. GLA has worker shoes upgrade and Cash Bounty general's power."
END

ACADEMY:buildmoregatherersold
"General, make sure that you have enough of Workers, Supply Trucks and Chinooks. Always increase your income. USA must have 2 Chinooks for each Supply Center, China - 4 Supply Trucks, GLA - 8 Workers."
END

ACADEMY:buildmoregatherers
"General, make sure that you have enough of Workers, Supply Trucks and Chinooks. Always increase your income. USA must have 2 Chinooks for each Supply Center, China - 2 Supply Trucks, GLA - 6 Workers."
END

ACADEMY:buildmorepeons
"Scouting is quite important. It helps determine which tactic should be used. Put scouts in front of your defenses. They will warn you about enemy attack in time. Move scouts in front of your attack force. They will warn you about danger. Don't forget that many scouts detect different types of stealth units. Detection capabilities are explained in unit descriptions. Read them attentively and use scouts properly."
END

ACADEMY:buildsupplycenterearlier
"When you play as GLA Stealth general, build fake units. They are a cheap distraction for your enemy. Do not underestimate this ability."
END

ACADEMY:buildtechstructuresooner
"For the advanced weaponry there is no replacement for a Strategy Center, Propaganda Center or Palace. Don't forget to build one a bit earlier in missions to ensure success."
END

ACADEMY:buildwarfactorysooner
"USA can highlight targets with target designator vehicles and some drones. Highlighting neutralizes stealth and gives damage bonus."
END

ACADEMY:clearbuildings
"Garrisoned buildings can be tough to handle - unless you know some tricks. Upgrade your USA Rangers with Flash Bangs, build GLA Toxin Tractors or Chinese Dragon Tanks to quickly clear out these strong points. The USA also can upgrade to the Bunker Buster to even clear out Tunnel Networks!"
END

ACADEMY:clearmines
"Demo Traps and mines can really be the start of a bad day. These sneaky tactics can be combated by using Dozers or Workers to clear these dangerous areas out."
END

ACADEMY:disguisedunits
"Try to rush in the very beginning. Build a small squad and attack your enemy as soon as possible. Such attack can cripple enemy economy and make further game easier."
END

ACADEMY:doubleclickattackmoveguard
"General, we have created a new way to direct your army. Simply select your units and double click the destination area. Your units will attack-move to the spot and then guard it. You may enable this through the options menu."
END

ACADEMY:eva
""
END

ACADEMY:firestorm
"Spend general's points to purchase powers which strengthen each other. For example, 3 powers: Tank Training + Tank Paradrop + Frenzy or 4 powers: Infantry Training + Infantry Paradrop + Cloning + Frenzy."
END

ACADEMY:garrionvehicle
"Some units may enter or steal other vehicles. Stealing vehicles with Hijackers or Suicide Bombers can allow you to sneak into enemy territory."
END

ACADEMY:idlebuildingunits
"Do not waste time. Build new forces while your main group attacks enemy base. Reinforce your attack group with new units during battle."
END

ACADEMY:multiplesupplycenters
"Use all available general's powers at once before attack. General's powers must weaken enemy defenses, while attack forces have to sneak through the breach and destroy the base."
END

ACADEMY:noincome
"When you reach 5th rank, the most powerful means of destruction become available: super weapons and super units. One super unit or one super weapon strike can level an entire base. This is why it is very important to have multiple bases in late game."
END

ACADEMY:pickstrategycenterplan
"USA can choose different battle plans depending on situation. Choose \"Bombardment\" battle plan when you attack enemy. Choose \"Hold the Line\" when you defend or when enemy uses his super weapon. \"Search And Destroy\" is useful when looking for survived enemy units and buildings."
END

ACADEMY:pickupsalvage
"The GLA is a sneaky bunch but they're also resourceful. Whenever the GLA units destroy another vehicle, a salvage bonus is left behind. Roll over the salvaged parts to upgrade your units, gain veterancy or get some extra cash. Salvage can make a big difference in a long fight so don't leave it just lying around. Salvage parts can be also created by Jarmen Kell and Salvage Drop general's power."
END

ACADEMY:ranoutofpower
"While GLA does not need power, USA and China consume it like popcorn. Build more power plants. Power production must be higher than power requirements. The loss of one or two power plants must not shut down entire base."
END

ACADEMY:researchupgrades
"Control the number of your units during battle. The bigger army you have - the less losses you sustain. Number of your units decreases during battle. When critical number is reached, you start to lose units too fast. It is better to catch this moment and retreat in time."
END

ACADEMY:spendgeneralspoints
"Don't try to attack strong enemy forces with single units. Gather at least a small group before attacking."
END

ACADEMY:stealthupgrade
"Many general's powers can be upgraded. USA can upgrade high explosive bomb to MOAB. GLA can upgrade toxin and acid bombs. China upgrades its bombs with black napalm. Tank general can upgrade Emergency Repair general's power."
END

ACADEMY:trybuildingradar
"If your base gets contaminated with toxins or radiation, clean it with USA Ambulance, China Biohazard Troopers or GLA BTR-50 Engineers. Neutron shells can clean toxins too, but you need to be careful with them."
END

ACADEMY:trycapturingstructures
"Do not turtle and sit in your base. Map control is very important. The more space you control - the more resources you have. Besides, you prevent enemy forces from moving freely across the map. Most of the maps have an important position in the center."
END

ACADEMY:trydragselectingunits
"Many new players like to use shapeless heaps of tanks or other units and don't care about losses. It is a bad idea for Contra. Each lost unit gives experience to your enemy. Enemy gains next rank faster. Next rank unlocks new technologies for him and allows to produce more powerful units. Spare your units, use them carefully, don't allow enemy to get experience."
END

ACADEMY:trygarrisoningastructure
"Soldiers can be effective on open space. But they are more effective when garrisoned. Garrison as many neutral buildings as possible. They will become your strong points."
END

ACADEMY:tryusingsuperweapons
"Super weapons are absolute means of destruction because it is impossible to defend from them. But they are expensive and reload for a long time. They can also be destroyed by airstrikes, general's powers and other super weapons. When you build super weapons, you get opportunity to destroy your enemy with ease but risk to lose both time and money without reaching any goals."
END

ACADEMY:unmannedvehicles
"General, some units can snipe or remove enemy drivers from vehicles. When this occurs, the vehicles become neutral and can be "borrowed" from the enemy. Feel free to go for a ride at your enemy's expense."
END

ACADEMY:usecontrolgroups
"Managing a large army can be a bit unruly sometimes. One way to manage lots of units easily is by creating a \"control group\". Simply select the group of units in question and press \"Ctrl\" & a number at the same time. Now anytime you press this number, the group of units will be selected. Tap the number twice quickly and the camera view will center over the group."
END

ACADEMY:useguardability
"Do not spend too much money for defense. It can be easily destroyed by artillery or aviation. Besides, many maps have multiple paths, which allow to avoid defenses and attack from the back."
END

ACADEMY:usesecondaryincomemethods
"General, acquiring supplies later in a mission can be difficult. Each faction has a unique way to gain funds during long battles. China can build Hackers and an Internet Center. You can direct the Hackers to hack the internet for funds anywhere or just send them inside Internet Center to gain money even quicker. The GLA depends on the Black Market and the USA relies on the Supply Drop. If you don't plan ahead, you may have shortages."
END

ACADEMY:useselectionhotkeys
"General, hotkeys are a great way to enhance your control of your forces. \"E\" will select all units of the same type on the view screen. If you tap \"E\" twice quickly, it will select all units of the same type across the entire battlefield. \"Q\" will select all your combat units on the map. \"W\" will select all your air units on the map. Give them a try, they'll help you out."
END

ACADEMY:usetunnelnetwork
"When it comes to the GLA sneaking around the battlefield is their calling card. Tunnel Networks offer defense capabilities but they also allow the player to move around quickly. Simply build a few Tunnel Networks and send your units inside. Click on the structure and you can expel them from any other Tunnel Network anywhere on the map. They are key to the overall GLA strategy."
END

